#2714
Southeast Stony Path~
     This thin trail encircles a small glade to the northwest. It is barely 
kept up, very much unlike the main highway. Rocks and burnt out shells of trees
lie along all sides of the path. The wind having blown smaller twigs and rocks 
into the path itself. It would appear to be some sort of game or hunting trail.
Though with the size of the stones along the path, some larger then a giant, 
which give the trail an almost tunnel like appearance you can hardly imagine 
what kind of animal would be stupid enough to allow itself to get trapped in 
here. From here the trail circles to the west and to the north.
~
