#2722
Within The Stone~
     The inside of this stone appears to be a cave that turns after a few feet
from the entrance, and heads north into darkness. The tunnel extends much
further then the outside of the stone ever possibly could in that direction.
Perhaps it is just a trick of the geography for the tunnel does slope downwards
at a rather extreme angle.
     A dim light calls to you from the depths of the rough hewn tunnel
flickering ominously in the distant cave. Even the dread, heated, light of the
eternal summer noon's day outside looks more inviting.
~
