#2764
The Halls of the Pantheon~
    You move westward, as far as you can, sensing no other direction to go but
back the way you came.  On and on you move, time losing all sense or meaning
until the 'hall' you are walking down ends. Not because you see the walls, but
simply because you feel you cannot go on. And as you sit there and rest,
considering going back, two doors, both black as midnight appear on the west
and the south walls.
~
